{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-angular-momentum","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-angular-momentum","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Angular momentum from the $\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)$ Casimir","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-momentum","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-casimir","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-nuclear-spin-parity"],"tags":["angular-momentum","q-deformed","su-q-2","casimir","spin","braid","jones-wenzl"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum","text":"q-angular-momentum.md","leanSource":"q-angular-momentum.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-angular-momentum\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K = \\hat{\\beta}</code> be a knot/link with braid representative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B_n</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-angular momentum</strong> is the eigenvalue of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Casimir element <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C_q</code> (the <a href=\"#def:q-casimir\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Casimir element</a>) on the spin-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j</code> irreducible of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  J_q^2(K) =  [j]_q  [j+1]_q\n  =  \\frac{q^j - q^{-j}}{q - q^{-1}} \\cdot\n        \\frac{q^{j+1} - q^{-(j+1)}}{q - q^{-1}}</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j</code> is the spin quantum number that the Jones--Wenzl projector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p_n</code> acting on the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-strand braid determines: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j = n/2</code> for the highest-weight component.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.md","heading":"Definition","number":"12.3.6","page":"b/def-q-angular-momentum","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":67},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.QAngularMomentum","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/q-angular-momentum.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
